# UNVERIFIED — pending debrief
#
# `int` is not a word in this language, and this is the case that says so
# (author decision 2026-08-12, `docs/panel/042`'s verdict section).
#
# It is the word every model reaches for and the one this milestone deleted.
# The reason is the thesis rather than taste: `int` carries forty years of
# conflicting widths — sixteen bits, thirty-two, sixty-four, arbitrary — so a
# reader must know the platform to know what it means, while `i64` is ambiguous
# to nobody. Panel 042's compiler-engineer vetoed the ALIAS on §4.15 grounds;
# deleting the word dissolved the veto rather than answering it, because with no
# alias there is no second spelling for `fmt` to choose between.
#
# The repair is a pure word-for-word swap, so it is `certain` and machine-
# applicable: `heroes check --in-place` migrates a whole file. That is not a
# convenience — 565 occurrences across 125 files were migrated by it during this
# milestone.
#
# Alone in its own file because the stages are gated: a lexer refusal stops the
# pipeline, so a file mixing this with a type error would only ever show this.

function main()
    n: int @ 1              #~ reserved_word
    print(n)
